- op: discuss  # f141
  at: '2026-10-12T14:12:21Z'  # f141
  by: agent  # f141
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f141
  clock: 3  # f141
  nonce: f141  # f141
  message: "Fixed in PR #1553 (merge 5364ca2eed; fix commit 927e6afd40). Root cause: a call on an in-repo type arrives keyed on the in-repo owner (App.Repo) while the catalogue keys the row on the library owner (Ecto.Repo), and nothing mapped one to the other; also USE_IMPLIED_BEHAVIOURS lacked Ecto.Repo, so 'use Ecto.Repo' produced no implements edge. Fix (language-neutral): new hypergumbo_core.owner_ancestry; finalize sub-step 7d stamps meta.external_owner_ancestors on unresolved calls whose owner (typed receiver / module slot / enclosing class of a bare-self call) is an in-repo type that does not declare the member, walking in-repo ancestors over extends/inherits/implements/includes nearest-first; io_boundary.classify_call_in_catalog and taint._match_propagation_entry retry with the owner-as-written then each ancestor before the short-name fallback. Ecto.Repo + HTTPoison.Base added to USE_IMPLIED_BEHAVIOURS (both __using__ declare @behaviour self, verified from deps source). Evidence (dev 5364ca2eed, filed fixture): 'hypergumbo io-boundaries <dir> --format json' -> db_read {Ecto.Repo.all:1, Ecto.Repo.stream:1}, db_write {Ecto.Repo.transaction:1}, external_potential only Enum.join/Enum.map; verify-claims db_read/db_write must_not_exist -> violated rc 1 (was inconclusive rc 2). Same mechanism proven by CLI tests for Python requests.Session subclass, Java FileInputStream subclass, JS net.Socket subclass. Corpus before/after (13 clones): plausible total_io_edges 698->1132 (434 Plausible.*Repo calls external_potential->db_read/db_write, spot-checked: all use Ecto.Repo); django +2 env_read (CommandParser(ArgumentParser).parse_known_args, correct); 11 others unchanged; 0 chains lost. Filed follow-ups: WI-gokun (elixir use-without-behaviour e.g. Tesla; HTTPoison.Base row verbs), WI-tafum (Spring Data rows), WI-fivor (ruby catalogue + ActiveRecord::Base qualifier), WI-basij (JS this.m() emits no edge)."  # f141
